exports[`check-integration-parity golden output > reports every rule violation in a disagreeing repository 1`] = `
{
  "status": 1,
  "stderr": "integration parity gate FAILED — 16 violation(s) over 5 server leaf face(s), 9 JS registration(s), 1 OpenRegister schema declaration file(s):
✗ [R1 render-pair] registerIntegration id "bravo" (src/bravo.js) declares renderMode "mount" but is missing the required \`unmount\` key — an incomplete render pair renders nothing on its surface (ADR-019 AD-11/AD-13, ADR-066 decision 7).
✗ [R2 id-correlation] a LeafDescriptor in lib/Leaf/Leaves.php declares no statically-readable \`id\` — a leaf whose id cannot be read cannot be correlated with its JS half.
✗ [R2 id-correlation] server leaf "charlie" (LeafDescriptor, lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) has NO matching registerIntegration({ id: 'charlie' }) in src/** — phantom leaf: the openregister.integrations.leaves capability advertises a surface that never mounts.
✗ [R2 id-correlation] registerIntegration id "delta" (src/bravo.js) has NO matching server-side face in lib/** (neither a \`new LeafDescriptor(id: 'delta')\` nor an IntegrationProvider whose getId() returns 'delta') — orphan registration: it mounts on window.OCA.OpenRegister.integrations but is invisible to the openregister.integrations.leaves capability.
✗ [R2 id-correlation] registerIntegration id "echo" (src/bravo.js) has NO matching server-side face in lib/** (neither a \`new LeafDescriptor(id: 'echo')\` nor an IntegrationProvider whose getId() returns 'echo') — orphan registration: it mounts on window.OCA.OpenRegister.integrations but is invisible to the openregister.integrations.leaves capability.
✗ [R3 renderMode] leaf "bravo" declares renderMode "component" server-side (lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) but "mount" in its JS registration (src/bravo.js) — a renderMode mismatch blanks the surface (ADR-066 decision 7).
✗ [R4 metadata] leaf "bravo" field \`label\` mismatch across layers: server (lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) says "Bravo", JS (src/bravo.js) says "Bravo2" — the two halves describe different leaves.
✗ [R4 metadata] leaf "bravo" field \`group\` mismatch across layers: server (lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) says "x", JS (src/bravo.js) says "y" — the two halves describe different leaves.
✗ [R4 metadata] leaf "bravo" field \`referenceType\` mismatch across layers: server (lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) says "r", JS (src/bravo.js) says "q" — the two halves describe different leaves.
✗ [R4 metadata] leaf "bravo" field \`surfaces\` mismatch across layers: server (lib/Leaf/Leaves.php) says ["tab"], JS (src/bravo.js) says ["widget"] — the two halves describe different leaves.
✗ [R5 spread-source] registerIntegration in src/bravo.js spreads \`...ghost\`, which is not imported in that file — the spread of an undefined binding registers a leaf with no id.
✗ [R5 spread-source] registerIntegration in src/bravo.js spreads \`...local\` imported from "./local", not from the leaf-owning package @conduction/nextcloud-vue — an override must extend the descriptor it overrides, or the id it registers under is not the one it thinks.
✗ [R5 spread-source] registerIntegration in src/bravo.js declares neither an \`id\` nor a spread of a descriptor — it registers a leaf with no identity.
✗ [R6 offlineConfig] leaf offlineConfig.plannedSchema = "nope" (src/bravo.js) names a schema this repo does not declare in lib/Settings/** — the leaf would query a schema that does not exist. Declared slugs: plan, ref
✗ [R6 offlineConfig] leaf offlineConfig.templateRefField = "gone" (src/bravo.js) is not a property of schema "plan" as declared in lib/Settings/** — the leaf would filter/display on a property that does not exist. Declared properties: date, title
✗ [R6 offlineConfig] leaf offlineConfig.titleField = "missing" (src/bravo.js) is not a property of schema "plan" as declared in lib/Settings/** — the leaf would filter/display on a property that does not exist. Declared properties: date, title

Assertions run per rule: R1:5 R2:8 R3:2 R4:7 R5:4 R7:0 R6:7
",
  "stdout": "",
}
`;
